  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "WordCraft（文档写作）",
      "text": "> 在智能体会话中起草、排版并交付可编辑的 Word 文档。保留章节结构、原生表格和页码，交付前重新打开核对。\n\n**版本**：0.1.0-dev.20261019.1 · **许可证**：Apache-2.0 · **技能**：16 个 · **MCP 服务**：1 个\n\n[English](README.en.md) · [安装](#安装) · [快速开始](#快速开始) · [项目结构](#项目结构)"
    },
    {
      "section": "项目定位",
      "text": "WordCraft 面向需要直接得到可编辑 Word 文档的用户，而不是一段 Markdown 或纯文本。它先收集并核对事实，再建立章节与字段结构，用原生标题、表格、页码和页眉页脚完成排版，最后重新打开文件检查读者实际看到的内容。\n\n适用场景：\n\n- 工作周报、会议纪要、项目说明\n- 商业报价、验收报告、需求说明\n- 简历、培训讲义、研究报告\n- 目录、页码、图表题注与样式统一\n- 已有文档的局部修改与版本比对\n\n不适用：\n\n- 把长文档简单拼接成一段文字\n- 在没有事实来源时编造业务数据\n- 用截图代替可编辑文档"
    },
    {
      "section": "一眼看懂",
      "text": "```text\n访谈 / 记录 / 数据 / 旧稿\n        │\n        ▼\nWordCraft 技能（收集 → 结构 → 排版 → 回读）"
    },
    {
      "section": "能力与边界",
      "text": "| 能力 | 说明 | 边界 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 起草 | 按目标、读者和材料生成章节 | 事实必须来自输入或明确标注 |\n| 结构 | 标题层级、目录、页码、页眉页脚 | 长文档分页需实际打开检查 |\n| 表格 | 原生表格、合并单元格、题注 | 复杂公式与图表需单独核对 |\n| 样式 | 段落、字体、编号、间距统一 | 不替代品牌设计规范 |\n| 局部修改 | 保留未涉及内容，只改指定范围 | 修改后必须重新打开 |\n| 版本比对 | 两版文字与结构差异 | 不判断业务上谁对 |\n| 导出 | DOCX，必要时 PDF | PDF 需检查字体嵌入 |"
    },
    {
      "section": "架构与核心流程",
      "text": "```text\n宿主 / Agent\n   │  调用技能\n   ▼\nskills/wordcraft-*  ──►  MCP 编辑器 / wordcraft-cli\n\n原则：\n\n1. 先确认目标、读者、篇幅和交付格式。\n2. 先生成结构，再填内容，最后统一排版。\n3. 每次修改保留可回退版本。\n4. 退出码成功不等于版面正确，必须重新打开检查。"
    },
    {
      "section": "兼容性",
      "text": "| 项目 | 状态 |\n|---|---|\n| 宿主 | Codex 有完整证据；其他宿主未验证 |\n| Node.js | 24+（编辑器） |\n| 原生引擎 | WordCraft 0.7.0 / wordcraft-cli |\n| 平台 | 以实际安装包与发行说明为准 |\n| Windows Git | 需要开启 longpaths |"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "```bash\ncodex plugin marketplace add partme-ai/full-aigc-plugins\ncodex plugin add wordcraft@full-aigc-plugins\n```\n\n安装后重启宿主，先做只读检查：\n\n> 打开这份文档，告诉我章节结构、页数和现有样式，不要修改。"
    },
    {
      "section": "快速开始",
      "text": "1. **确认目标**：文档类型、读者、篇幅、必须包含的章节。\n2. **收集事实**：会议记录、数据、旧稿、品牌规范。\n3. **生成结构**：先目录和章节，再逐节填内容。\n4. **统一排版**：标题、正文、表格、页码、页眉页脚。\n5. **重新打开**：检查分页、目录、表格跨页和字体。\n6. **交付**：给出 DOCX，必要时导出 PDF。"
    },
    {
      "section": "配置",
      "text": "| 变量 | 用途 | 默认 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CRAFT_WORKSPACE_ROOT` | 编辑器绑定的工作区 | 当前项目 |\n| `CRAFT_EDITOR_UPDATE` | 设为 `off` 跳过增强包下载 | 开启 |\n\n不要在文档或配置中写入密钥、令牌和私有路径。"
    },
    {
      "section": "扩展契约",
      "text": "新增技能时应：\n\n- 使用 `wordcraft-` 前缀\n- 在 `SKILL.md` 声明触发条件和边界\n- 通过 MCP 或固定 CLI 操作真实文档\n- 修改后重新打开并核对结构\n- 不把“生成成功”写成“交付完成”"
    },
    {
      "section": "重试、幂等与恢复",
      "text": "- 修改前保存版本或副本。\n- 失败后先检查当前文档状态，不自动重复写入。\n- 重新执行时使用新输出路径。\n- 不确定的结果标记为待核对。"
    },
    {
      "section": "数据与状态",
      "text": "- 原始材料只读。\n- 输出文档与临时文件分开。\n- 保留修改记录和最终版本。\n- 删除临时文件前确认交付文件已保存。"
    },
    {
      "section": "安全",
      "text": "- 不把未授权材料上传到第三方服务。\n- 敏感字段脱敏后再交付。\n- 宏、外部链接和嵌入对象需显式确认。\n- 发现泄露先轮换凭据，再清理文档。"
    },
    {
      "section": "可观测性与运行",
      "text": "- 记录命令、输出文件、页数和结构检查结果。\n- 交付前确认文件可打开、目录可更新、页码正确。\n- 长文档至少抽查首页、中间页和末页。"
    },
    {
      "section": "开发与验证",
      "text": "```bash\nnode --test\npython3 -m pytest\n```\n\n提交前确认技能清单、目录和 README 一致。"
    },
    {
      "section": "打包与发布",
      "text": "- 版本与 `plugin.json`、市场清单、tag 一致。\n- ZIP 根目录为 `wordcraft-plugin`。\n- 发布后重新安装并做一次只读检查。"
    },
    {
      "section": "升级与迁移",
      "text": "- 升级前备份工作区文档。\n- 旧版本生成的文件保持可打开。\n- 迁移后重新检查模板、页码和目录。"
    },
    {
      "section": "故障排查",
      "text": "| 现象 | 检查 |\n|---|---|\n| 文档打不开 | 文件是否完整、是否被占用 |\n| 目录不更新 | 在 Word 中更新域 |\n| 页码错乱 | 分节符与页码起始值 |\n| 表格跨页异常 | 行属性与重复标题行 |\n| 字体缺失 | 嵌入字体或替换字体 |"
    },
    {
      "section": "项目结构",
      "text": "```text\nwordcraft-plugin/\n├── .zcode-plugin/      # ZCode 清单与 UI surface\n├── .codex-plugin/      # Codex 清单\n├── .claude-plugin/     # Claude 清单"
    },
    {
      "section": "深入文档",
      "text": "- [架构](docs/architecture.zh-CN.md)\n- [场景技能](docs/scene-skills.md)\n- [任务回执](docs/task-receipts.zh-CN.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "贡献与支持",
      "text": "提交问题时附上插件版本、宿主、文档类型、命令、输出文件和预期结果。不要附真实敏感文档。"
    },
    {
      "section": "许可证",
      "text": "Apache-2.0，见 [LICENSE](LICENSE)。"
    },
    {
      "section": "WordCraft (Document Writing)",
      "text": "> Draft, lay out, and deliver editable Word documents from an agent session. Keep real section structures, native tables, and page numbers, then reopen the file before handoff.\n\n**Version**: 0.1.0-dev.20261019.1 · **License**: Apache-2.0 · **Skills**: 16 · **MCP server**: 1\n\n[简体中文](README.md) · [Install](#installation) · [Quick start](#quick-start) · [Project layout](#project-layout)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Positioning",
      "text": "WordCraft is for users who need an editable Word document, not Markdown or plain text. It collects and checks facts, builds a section and field structure, lays the result out with native headings, tables, page numbers, and headers, then reopens the file to check what the reader will see.\n\nUse it for:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Positioning",
      "text": "- Weekly reports, meeting minutes, project briefs\n- Business proposals, acceptance reports, requirements\n- Resumes, training material, research reports\n- Consistent TOC, page numbers, captions, and styles\n- Local edits and version comparison\n\nDo not use it for:\n\n- Concatenating a long document into one text block\n- Inventing business data without a source\n- Replacing an editable document with screenshots"
    },
    {
      "section": "At a glance",
      "text": "```text\ninterviews / notes / data / old drafts\n        │\n        ▼\nWordCraft skill (collect → structure → layout → read back)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Capabilities and boundaries",
      "text": "| Capability | What it does | Boundary |\n|---|---|---|\n| Draft | Build sections for the audience and goal | Facts must come from input or be labeled |\n| Structure | Heading levels, TOC, page numbers, headers | Long-document pagination needs a real open |\n| Tables | Native tables, merged cells, captions | Complex formulas and charts need separate checks |\n| Styles | Consistent paragraphs, fonts, numbering, spacing | Not a brand-design system |\n| Local edits | Change only the requested scope | Reopen after every edit |\n| Version comparison | Text and structural differences | Does not decide which version is business-correct |\n| Export | DOCX, and PDF when needed | PDF needs font-embedding checks |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture and core flow",
      "text": "```text\nHost / agent\n   │  invokes a skill\n   ▼\nskills/wordcraft-*  ──►  MCP editor / wordcraft-cli\n\nRules:\n\n1. Confirm goal, audience, length, and delivery format first.\n2. Build structure before content; unify layout last.\n3. Keep a rollback version for every edit.\n4. Exit code 0 is not proof of correct layout; reopen and check."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Item | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Host | Codex has full evidence; other hosts are NOT_RUN |\n| Node.js | 24+ (editor) |\n| Native engine | WordCraft 0.7.0 / wordcraft-cli |\n| Platforms | Follow the actual package and release notes |\n| Windows Git | Enable longpaths |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "```bash\ncodex plugin marketplace add partme-ai/full-aigc-plugins\ncodex plugin add wordcraft@full-aigc-plugins\n```\n\nRestart the host and start read-only:\n\n> Open this document and report its section structure, page count, and current styles. Do not modify it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "1. **Confirm the goal**: type, audience, length, required sections.\n2. **Collect facts**: notes, data, old drafts, brand rules.\n3. **Build structure**: TOC and sections first, then content.\n4. **Unify layout**: headings, body, tables, page numbers, headers.\n5. **Reopen**: check pagination, TOC, table breaks, and fonts.\n6. **Deliver**: DOCX, plus PDF when required."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Variable | Purpose | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CRAFT_WORKSPACE_ROOT` | Workspace bound to the editor | current project |\n| `CRAFT_EDITOR_UPDATE` | Set to `off` to skip the enhanced editor download | enabled |\n\nNever write secrets, tokens, or private paths into documents or configuration."
    },
    {
      "section": "Extension contract",
      "text": "When adding a skill:\n\n- Use the `wordcraft-` prefix\n- Declare triggers and boundaries in `SKILL.md`\n- Operate on a real document through MCP or the pinned CLI\n- Reopen and verify structure after every edit\n- Never describe generation as completed delivery"
    },
    {
      "section": "Retry, idempotency, and recovery",
      "text": "- Save a version or copy before editing.\n- After a failure, inspect the current document; do not replay writes.\n- Retry with a new output path.\n- Mark uncertain results for review."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data and state",
      "text": "- Source material is read-only.\n- Outputs and temporary files are separate.\n- Keep edit history and the final version.\n- Confirm the deliverable is saved before deleting temporary files."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security",
      "text": "- Do not upload unauthorized material to third-party services.\n- Redact sensitive fields before delivery.\n- Explicitly confirm macros, external links, and embedded objects.\n- On a suspected leak, rotate credentials before cleaning documents."
    },
    {
      "section": "Observability and operation",
      "text": "- Record command, output file, page count, and structure checks.\n- Before delivery, confirm the file opens, the TOC updates, and page numbers are correct.\n- For long documents, sample the first, middle, and last pages."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and verification",
      "text": "```bash\nnode --test\npython3 -m pytest\n```\n\nBefore committing, confirm the skill inventory, directories, and README agree."
    },
    {
      "section": "Packaging and release",
      "text": "- Version matches `plugin.json`, marketplace manifests, and the tag.\n- The ZIP root is `wordcraft-plugin`.\n- After release, reinstall and run one read-only inspection."
    },
    {
      "section": "Upgrade and migration",
      "text": "- Back up workspace documents before upgrading.\n- Files from older versions must remain openable.\n- Recheck templates, page numbers, and TOC after migration."
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting",
      "text": "| Symptom | Check |\n|---|---|\n| Document will not open | File integrity or file lock |\n| TOC is stale | Update fields in Word |\n| Page numbers wrong | Section breaks and page-number start |\n| Table breaks badly | Row properties and repeat-header |\n| Missing fonts | Embed or substitute fonts |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Project layout",
      "text": "```text\nwordcraft-plugin/\n├── .zcode-plugin/      # ZCode manifest and UI surface\n├── .codex-plugin/      # Codex manifest\n├── .claude-plugin/     # Claude manifest"
    },
    {
      "section": "Deep links",
      "text": "- [Architecture](docs/architecture.md)\n- [Scene skills](docs/scene-skills.md)\n- [Task receipts](docs/task-receipts.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing and support",
      "text": "Include plugin version, host, document type, command, output file, and expected result. Do not attach sensitive documents."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
